<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said ibn Harun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said ibn Harun was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of Santa María del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a>, a small Muslim kingdom around present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Faro</a> in southern Portugal. Around 1018, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> broke apart, this member of a local Arab family made himself independent in the coastal town and its district. His family, the Banu Harun, gave the town its medieval name and ruled it until the Taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> absorbed it in the mid-11th century.</p></div>
